{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01XLVwQkmUNgC1vKnsAp3JwW","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tslug: pose-review-brief-templates-are-immutable\n3\tstatus: in-progress\n4\tcreated_at: 2026-11-09\n5\tcompleted_at:\n6\tsupersedes:\n7\tdepends_on: pose-delegated-approval-survives-routine-drift\n8\tremediates:\n9\tpriority: 1\n10\tcomponents: pose-mcp\n11\ttask_type: bugfix\n12\tdelivers: capability:review-brief-templates-are-immutable\n13\t---\n14\t\n15\t# Spec: A review brief template version never changes its text\n16\t\n17\t## 1. Intent\n18\t\n19\t### Goal\n20\t\n21\tA change to the text a review brief template renders takes a new template version, and the build fails when it does not.\n22\t\n23\t### Business value\n24\t\n25\tA run records the digest of the brief it was sent and its proof signs it, so the text a template version renders is part of what that version means. `review-brief/4` changed its text three times under one version while the conclusion rules were being stated, and the runs briefed with its earlier texts could no longer be re-rendered: their approvals failed verification (\"brief/template/notes/transmitted bytes differ\") until the retention of delegated approvals stopped re-rendering the brief for a done scope. Nothing guarded the rule that a version is immutable; the mistake was caught by measuring, not by the build. This closes the follow-up of `pose-delegated-approval-survives-routine-drift`.\n26\t\n27\t### Constraints\n28\t\n29\t- The mechanisms are the existing ones: the template versions and the list of earlier templates, and a test in `internal/pose` with a golden file.\n30\t- The guard may not make an honest new version hard: a new version records its digest once, and a recorded digest is never rewritten by the tooling.\n31\t\n32\t### Non-goals\n33\t\n34\t- Changing any template's text.\n35\t- The adjudication and smoke templates, whose versions did not change under one name.\n36\t\n37\t## 2. Requirements\n38\t\n39\t### Functional\n40\t\n41\t- R1: Every review brief template version in use (the current one and every earlier one a run may have been briefed with) shall have a recorded digest of the text it renders from fixed bundles that carry every kind of content a brief renders: bare, with implementer notes, structural facts (one shared with another spec) and a tool scoped to a component, and as the second round with its predecessor run and bundle, an unreadable draft and an open finding, and as a third round with nothing open; with a renamed entry, an optional criterion and notes that carry a fence.\n42\t- R2: A test shall fail when a version renders text whose digest differs from the recorded one, and its message shall say that a change to the text takes a new version.\n43\t- R3: A version in use without a recorded digest shall fail the test, so a new version cannot be published unrecorded.\n44\t- R4: Recording a digest shall never rewrite one already recorded.\n45\t- R5: The rendering from the fixed bundle shall be deterministic.\n46\t\n47\t### Non-functional\n48\t\n49\t- No change to what any brief renders, to a bundle, a run or a policy.\n50\t\n51\t### Security\n52\t\n53\t- None: the guard protects the verifiability of runs already given.\n54\t\n55\t### Compatibility\n56\t\n57\t- The recorded digests are those of the versions as they render today. Runs briefed with an earlier text of `review-brief/4` are already verified as sealed by the retention of delegated approvals, which does not re-render the brief.\n58\t\n59\t## 3. Technical Plan\n60\t\n61\t### Affected areas\n62\t\n63\t`internal/pose` tests and `testdata`, the ADR on delegated review conclusions, the manual.\n64\t\n65\t### Artifacts\n66\t\n67\t- created: .pose/specs/2026-11-09-pose-review-brief-templates-are-immutable.md\n68\t- created: .pose/starts/pose-review-brief-templates-are-immutable.json\n69\t- created: .pose/changelogs/unreleased/pose-review-brief-templates-are-immutable.md\n70\t- modified: .pose/indexes/validation-matrix.json\n71\t- created: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_brief_versions_test.go\n72\t- created: pose-mcp/internal/pose/testdata/review_brief_template_digests.json\n73\t- modified: POSE.md\n74\t- modified: locales/pt-BR/POSE.md\n75\t- modified: pose-mcp/internal/scaffold/dist/POSE.md\n76\t- modified: pose-mcp/internal/scaffold/dist/locales/pt-BR/POSE.md\n77\t\n78\t### Delivery targets\n79\t\n80\t- capability:review-brief-templates-are-immutable module:pose-mcp profile:composed-capability entrypoint:pose-mcp/cmd/pose/main.go\n81\t\n82\t### API/contract changes\n83\t\n84\tNone. A rule of the repository: the text of a published template version is frozen.\n85\t\n86\t## 4. Tasks\n87\t\n88\t- [x] Render each version from a fixed bundle and record the digests\n89\t- [x] Fail the build when a version renders other text, and when a version has no digest\n90\t- [x] See the guard fail on an edited sentence and pass when it is reverted\n91\t- [x] Say it in the manual\n92\t- [ ] Independent review and closeout\n93\t\n94\t## 5. Decisions\n95\t\n96\t### Decision D1\n97\t- Basis: R1, R2, R3, R4\n98\t- Minimal option: a comment on the constants asking not to edit a version\n99\t- Selected option: a golden digest per version, recorded once, checked by the build\n100\t- Rationale: the rule was already known and was broken three times in one afternoon; a comment is not read at the moment a sentence is added, a failing build is\n101\t- Consequences: a text change takes a new version, its digest is recorded once and the earlier version keeps rendering\n102\t- Falsifier: a change to the text of a published version that the build accepts\n103\t\n104\t## 6. Validation\n105\t\n106\t### Strategy\n107\t\n108\tThe test was written, then a sentence of `review-brief/4` was edited to see it fail with the message naming the version, and reverted to see it pass.\n109\t\n110\t### Deterministic checks\n111\t\n112\t`go test` of the tests named in the trace; the strict matrix in a clean clone.\n113\t\n114\t### Requirement trace\n115\t- R1 [satisfied] test:TestEveryReviewBriefTemplateVersionRendersWhatItRenderedWhenItWasPublished check:review-brief-templates-are-immutable-integration\n116\t- R2 [satisfied] test:TestEveryReviewBriefTemplateVersionRendersWhatItRenderedWhenItWasPublished\n117\t- R3 [satisfied] test:TestEveryReviewBriefTemplateVersionRendersWhatItRenderedWhenItWasPublished\n118\t- R4 [satisfied] test:TestEveryReviewBriefTemplateVersionRendersWhatItRenderedWhenItWasPublished\n119\t- R5 [satisfied] test:TestTheDigestSeesEverySectionOfEveryVariant\n120\t\n121\t### Known gaps\n122\t- The versioned handoff renderers (`delegation_handoff.go`) and the adjudication and smoke templates sign text under a version name too and are not covered; the follow-up below names them.\n123\t- A recorded version that is removed from the list of earlier templates fails the test, and the recording refuses to overwrite a digest file it cannot read or parse.\n124\t- The adjudication and smoke templates are not covered: their versions did not change under one name, and they render from scripts and questions the fixed bundle does not carry.\n125\t- The digest of `review-brief/4` is the text as it renders today; the two earlier texts it had before are not recorded and are not needed, since a done scope's approval is verified as sealed.\n126\t- The recording is made with `UPDATE_BRIEF_GOLDEN=1` and keeps every digest already in the file; changing one by hand is visible in review.\n127\t\n128\t---\n129\t\n130\t## 7. Final Report\n131\t\n132\t### Delivered scope\n133\tEach review brief template version in use has a digest of what it renders from a fixed bundle, recorded in `testdata/review_brief_template_digests.json`; the build fails when a version renders other text, saying that a change takes a new version, and when a version has no digest; recording never rewrites a digest already there. Left out: the adjudication and smoke templates.\n134\t\n135\t### Files and modules changed\n136\t- pose-mcp/internal/pose (review_brief_versions_test.go, testdata/review_brief_template_digests.json)\n137\t- POSE.md and its pt-BR and scaffold copies; the validation matrix gains `review-brief-templates-are-immutable-integration`\n138\t\n139\t### Validation executed\n140\t- Command: `pose validate --strict --jobs 4` on a clean clone of the reviewed head, and the suites of `internal/pose`\n141\t- Result: recorded by the sealed validation evidence; independent delegated review (Claude Opus 5.5, independent by model) concluded with `pose review conclude`.\n142\t\n143\t### Residual risks\n144\t- A text change that also changes the version constants and the digests in one commit passes by design: the guard asks for a new version, not for a reviewer.\n145\t\n146\t### Follow-ups\n147\t\n148\t- [open] Cover the adjudication and smoke brief templates and the versioned delegation handoff renderers with the same golden digests, rendered from a fixed script, fixed questions and a fixed predecessor run. (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:low review:2027-01-08)\n149\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"[private-session]","uuid":"550dc06e-9075-442c-91a0-1aca2bdbff52","timestamp":"2026-11-09T12:08:25.332Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-4103419841/worktree/.pose/specs/2026-11-09-pose-review-brief-templates-are-immutable.md","content":"---\nslug: pose-review-brief-templates-are-immutable\nstatus: in-progress\ncreated_at: 2026-11-09\ncompleted_at:\nsupersedes:\ndepends_on: pose-delegated-approval-survives-routine-drift\nremediates:\npriority: 1\ncomponents: pose-mcp\ntask_type: bugfix\ndelivers: capability:review-brief-templates-are-immutable\n---\n\n# Spec: A review brief template version never changes its text\n\n## 1. Intent\n\n### Goal\n\nA change to the text a review brief template renders takes a new template version, and the build fails when it does not.\n\n### Business value\n\nA run records the digest of the brief it was sent and its proof signs it, so the text a template version renders is part of what that version means. `review-brief/4` changed its text three times under one version while the conclusion rules were being stated, and the runs briefed with its earlier texts could no longer be re-rendered: their approvals failed verification (\"brief/template/notes/transmitted bytes differ\") until the retention of delegated approvals stopped re-rendering the brief for a done scope. Nothing guarded the rule that a version is immutable; the mistake was caught by measuring, not by the build. This closes the follow-up of `pose-delegated-approval-survives-routine-drift`.\n\n### Constraints\n\n- The mechanisms are the existing ones: the template versions and the list of earlier templates, and a test in `internal/pose` with a golden file.\n- The guard may not make an honest new version hard: a new version records its digest once, and a recorded digest is never rewritten by the tooling.\n\n### Non-goals\n\n- Changing any template's text.\n- The adjudication and smoke templates, whose versions did not change under one name.\n\n## 2. Requirements\n\n### Functional\n\n- R1: Every review brief template version in use (the current one and every earlier one a run may have been briefed with) shall have a recorded digest of the text it renders from fixed bundles that carry every kind of content a brief renders: bare, with implementer notes, structural facts (one shared with another spec) and a tool scoped to a component, and as the second round with its predecessor run and bundle, an unreadable draft and an open finding, and as a third round with nothing open; with a renamed entry, an optional criterion and notes that carry a fence.\n- R2: A test shall fail when a version renders text whose digest differs from the recorded one, and its message shall say that a change to the text takes a new version.\n- R3: A version in use without a recorded digest shall fail the test, so a new version cannot be published unrecorded.\n- R4: Recording a digest shall never rewrite one already recorded.\n- R5: The rendering from the fixed bundle shall be deterministic.\n\n### Non-functional\n\n- No change to what any brief renders, to a bundle, a run or a policy.\n\n### Security\n\n- None: the guard protects the verifiability of runs already given.\n\n### Compatibility\n\n- The recorded digests are those of the versions as they render today. Runs briefed with an earlier text of `review-brief/4` are already verified as sealed by the retention of delegated approvals, which does not re-render the brief.\n\n## 3. Technical Plan\n\n### Affected areas\n\n`internal/pose` tests and `testdata`, the ADR on delegated review conclusions, the manual.\n\n### Artifacts\n\n- created: .pose/specs/2026-11-09-pose-review-brief-templates-are-immutable.md\n- created: .pose/starts/pose-review-brief-templates-are-immutable.json\n- created: .pose/changelogs/unreleased/pose-review-brief-templates-are-immutable.md\n- modified: .pose/indexes/validation-matrix.json\n- created: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_brief_versions_test.go\n- created: pose-mcp/internal/pose/testdata/review_brief_template_digests.json\n- modified: POSE.md\n- modified: locales/pt-BR/POSE.md\n- modified: pose-mcp/internal/scaffold/dist/POSE.md\n- modified: pose-mcp/internal/scaffold/dist/locales/pt-BR/POSE.md\n\n### Delivery targets\n\n- capability:review-brief-templates-are-immutable module:pose-mcp profile:composed-capability entrypoint:pose-mcp/cmd/pose/main.go\n\n### API/contract changes\n\nNone. A rule of the repository: the text of a published template version is frozen.\n\n## 4. Tasks\n\n- [x] Render each version from a fixed bundle and record the digests\n- [x] Fail the build when a version renders other text, and when a version has no digest\n- [x] See the guard fail on an edited sentence and pass when it is reverted\n- [x] Say it in the manual\n- [ ] Independent review and closeout\n\n## 5. Decisions\n\n### Decision D1\n- Basis: R1, R2, R3, R4\n- Minimal option: a comment on the constants asking not to edit a version\n- Selected option: a golden digest per version, recorded once, checked by the build\n- Rationale: the rule was already known and was broken three times in one afternoon; a comment is not read at the moment a sentence is added, a failing build is\n- Consequences: a text change takes a new version, its digest is recorded once and the earlier version keeps rendering\n- Falsifier: a change to the text of a published version that the build accepts\n\n## 6. Validation\n\n### Strategy\n\nThe test was written, then a sentence of `review-brief/4` was edited to see it fail with the message naming the version, and reverted to see it pass.\n\n### Deterministic checks\n\n`go test` of the tests named in the trace; the strict matrix in a clean clone.\n\n### Requirement trace\n- R1 [satisfied] test:TestEveryReviewBriefTemplateVersionRendersWhatItRenderedWhenItWasPublished check:review-brief-templates-are-immutable-integration\n- R2 [satisfied] test:TestEveryReviewBriefTemplateVersionRendersWhatItRenderedWhenItWasPublished\n- R3 [satisfied] test:TestEveryReviewBriefTemplateVersionRendersWhatItRenderedWhenItWasPublished\n- R4 [satisfied] test:TestEveryReviewBriefTemplateVersionRendersWhatItRenderedWhenItWasPublished\n- R5 [satisfied] test:TestTheDigestSeesEverySectionOfEveryVariant\n\n### Known gaps\n- The versioned handoff renderers (`delegation_handoff.go`) and the adjudication and smoke templates sign text under a version name too and are not covered; the follow-up below names them.\n- A recorded version that is removed from the list of earlier templates fails the test, and the recording refuses to overwrite a digest file it cannot read or parse.\n- The adjudication and smoke templates are not covered: their versions did not change under one name, and they render from scripts and questions the fixed bundle does not carry.\n- The digest of `review-brief/4` is the text as it renders today; the two earlier texts it had before are not recorded and are not needed, since a done scope's approval is verified as sealed.\n- The recording is made with `UPDATE_BRIEF_GOLDEN=1` and keeps every digest already in the file; changing one by hand is visible in review.\n\n---\n\n## 7. Final Report\n\n### Delivered scope\nEach review brief template version in use has a digest of what it renders from a fixed bundle, recorded in `testdata/review_brief_template_digests.json`; the build fails when a version renders other text, saying that a change takes a new version, and when a version has no digest; recording never rewrites a digest already there. Left out: the adjudication and smoke templates.\n\n### Files and modules changed\n- pose-mcp/internal/pose (review_brief_versions_test.go, testdata/review_brief_template_digests.json)\n- POSE.md and its pt-BR and scaffold copies; the validation matrix gains `review-brief-templates-are-immutable-integration`\n\n### Validation executed\n- Command: `pose validate --strict --jobs 4` on a clean clone of the reviewed head, and the suites of `internal/pose`\n- Result: recorded by the sealed validation evidence; independent delegated review (Claude Opus 5.5, independent by model) concluded with `pose review conclude`.\n\n### Residual risks\n- A text change that also changes the version constants and the digests in one commit passes by design: the guard asks for a new version, not for a reviewer.\n\n### Follow-ups\n\n- [open] Cover the adjudication and smoke brief templates and the versioned delegation handoff renderers with the same golden digests, rendered from a fixed script, fixed questions and a fixed predecessor run. (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:low review:2027-01-08)\n","numLines":149,"startLine":1,"totalLines":149}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01XLVwQkmUNgC1vKnsAp3JwW","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgsKySLgxrysod9xLs9gK","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01L5FVXPX5uMB5UP52vgiWiF","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-4103419841/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_brief_versions_test.go"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1779,"cache_read_input_tokens":16370,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1779},"output_tokens":7,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"[private-session]","uuid":"eddc9686-fe14-4e6c-9da5-a0bd0d0f0a27","timestamp":"2026-11-09T12:08:25.928Z","request_id":"req_011CgsKyS6oq2gN9Yr1hduQt","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01L5FVXPX5uMB5UP52vgiWiF":{"file_path":"/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-4103419841/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_brief_versions_test.go"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01L5FVXPX5uMB5UP52vgiWiF","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tpackage pose\n2\t\n3\timport (\n4\t\t\"crypto/sha256\"\n5\t\t\"encoding/hex\"\n6\t\t\"encoding/json\"\n7\t\t\"os\"\n8\t\t\"sort\"\n9\t\t\"strings\"\n10\t\t\"testing\"\n11\t)\n12\t\n13\t// Spec pose-review-brief-templates-are-immutable.\n14\t//\n15\t// A run records the digest of the brief it was sent, and its proof signs it. The text a\n16\t// template version renders is therefore part of what that version means: change the text\n17\t// and every run briefed with the version can no longer be re-rendered. The text of\n18\t// review-brief/4 changed three times under one version in this repository, before this\n19\t// guard. A golden digest of what each version renders, from a fixed bundle, makes a text\n20\t// change fail the build until it takes a new version.\n21\t\n22\tconst reviewBriefGoldenPath = \"testdata/review_brief_template_digests.json\"\n23\t\n24\t// fixedBriefBundle is a bundle with every kind of content a review brief renders, and\n25\t// nothing that varies between runs.\n26\tfunc fixedBriefBundle() ReviewBundle {\n27\t\tvar bundle ReviewBundle\n28\t\tbundle.BundleID = \"rvb-0000000000000001\"\n29\t\tbundle.BundleDigest = \"sha256:\" + strings.Repeat(\"a\", 64)\n30\t\tbundle.Payload.Scope = ReviewBundleScope{Ref: \"spec:fixed\", Kind: \"spec\", Slug: \"fixed\", Components: []string{\"core\"}, Deliveries: []string{\"capability:fixed\"}}\n31\t\tbundle.Payload.Subject.Entries = []ReviewBundleSubjectEntry{{Action: \"modified\", Path: \"core/a.go\", Class: \"source\", Digest: \"sha256:\" + strings.Repeat(\"b\", 64), Reason: \"changed\"}}\n32\t\tbundle.Payload.Plan.Independence = \"different-actor\"\n33\t\tbundle.Payload.Plan.Criteria = []ReviewPlanCriterion{\n34\t\t\t{ID: \"correctness\", Description: \"The behavior is correct.\", Required: true, Kind: ReviewCriterionKindMechanical, EvidenceClasses: []string{\"unit\"}},\n35\t\t\t{ID: \"design-causality\", Description: \"The design is explained.\", Required: true, Kind: ReviewCriterionKindJudgment},\n36\t\t}\n37\t\tbundle.Payload.Plan.Tools = []ReviewPlanTool{\n38\t\t\t{ID: \"artifact-check\", Requiredness: \"required\", Args: []string{\"pose\", \"artifact-check\", \"--spec\", \"fixed\"}},\n39\t\t\t{ID: \"surface-check\", Requiredness: \"required\", Args: []string{\"pose\", \"surface-check\"}, EvidenceClasses: []string{\"integration\", \"reachability\"}},\n40\t\t\t{ID: \"assess-design\", Requiredness: \"recommended\", Args: []string{\"pose\", \"assess\", \"design\"}},\n41\t\t}\n42\t\tbundle.Payload.Evidence = []ReviewBundleEvidence{{ID: \"core/go/test\", Module: \"core\", Check: \"test\", EvidenceClass: \"unit\", Outcome: \"pass\"}}\n43\t\treturn bundle\n44\t}\n45\t\n46\t// richBriefBundle adds what only some briefs carry: structural facts (one shared with another\n47\t// spec) and a tool scoped to a component.\n48\tfunc richBriefBundle() ReviewBundle {\n49\t\tbundle := fixedBriefBundle()\n50\t\tbundle.Payload.Plan.Structure = &ReviewPlanStructure{Material: []ReviewStructuralFact{\n51\t\t\t{ID: \"SD-aaaa1111\", Kind: \"governance-contract\", Action: \"changed\", Subject: \"an ADR\"},\n52\t\t\t{ID: \"SD-bbbb2222\", Kind: \"api-contract\", Action: \"added\", Subject: \"an endpoint\", SharedWith: []string{\"other-spec\"}},\n53\t\t}}\n54\t\tbundle.Payload.Plan.Tools = append(bundle.Payload.Plan.Tools, ReviewPlanTool{ID: \"assess-discover\", Component: \"core\", Requiredness: \"recommended\", Args: []string{\"pose\", \"assess\", \"discover\"}})\n55\t\tbundle.Payload.Subject.Entries = append(bundle.Payload.Subject.Entries, ReviewBundleSubjectEntry{Action: \"renamed\", OldPath: \"core/old.go\", NewPath: \"core/new.go\", Class: \"source\", Reason: \"moved\"})\n56\t\tbundle.Payload.Plan.Criteria = append(bundle.Payload.Plan.Criteria, ReviewPlanCriterion{ID: \"documentation\", Description: \"The docs say it.\", Required: false, Kind: ReviewCriterionKindMechanical})\n57\t\treturn bundle\n58\t}\n59\t\n60\t// renderFixedBriefs renders a template every way a brief can differ: bare, with implementer\n61\t// notes and structural facts, and as the second round with an open finding of the first. A\n62\t// sentence of any section, in any of them, changes the digest.\n63\tfunc renderFixedBriefs(template string) string {\n64\t\tconclusion := reviewBriefAsksConclusion(template)\n65\t\tvar out []string\n66\t\trounds := []*ReviewRound{nil}\n67\t\tif template != reviewBriefTemplateFirst {\n68\t\t\tprior := &ReviewRun{RunID: \"rrn-prior0000000001\", BundleID: \"rvb-prior0000000001\", Output: \"decision: changes-requested\"}\n69\t\t\tpriorBundle := fixedBriefBundle()\n70\t\t\tpriorBundle.Payload.Subject.Head = \"0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef01234567\"\n71\t\t\trounds = []*ReviewRound{\n72\t\t\t\t{Number: 1},\n73\t\t\t\t{Number: 2, Prior: prior, PriorBundle: &priorBundle, Broken: \"a draft of round 1 could not be read\", Open: []ReviewOpenFinding{{ID: \"B1\", Round: 1, Severity: \"medium\", Disposition: \"blocker\", File: \"core/a.go\", Line: 3, Summary: \"a defect\", Carried: \"F1\"}}},\n74\t\t\t\t{Number: 3},\n75\t\t\t}\n76\t\t}\n77\t\tfor _, round := range rounds {\n78\t\t\tout = append(out, renderReviewBriefBody(fixedBriefBundle(), ReviewBriefKindReview, template, \"\", nil, round, conclusion, nil))\n79\t\t\tout = append(out, renderReviewBriefBody(richBriefBundle(), ReviewBriefKindReview, template, \"Implementer note.\\n```\\na fence in the notes\\n```\\nSecond line.\", nil, round, conclusion, nil))\n80\t\t}\n81\t\treturn strings.Join(out, \"\\n=====\\n\")\n82\t}\n83\t\n84\tfunc briefTemplateDigest(template string) string {\n85\t\tsum := sha256.Sum256([]byte(renderFixedBriefs(template)))\n86\t\treturn \"sha256:\" + hex.EncodeToString(sum[:])\n87\t}\n88\t\n89\tfunc briefTemplatesInUse() []string {\n90\t\tversions := append([]string{reviewBriefTemplateConclusions}, reviewBriefEarlierTemplates...)\n91\t\tsort.Strings(versions)\n92\t\treturn versions\n93\t}\n94\t\n95\tfunc TestEveryReviewBriefTemplateVersionRendersWhatItRenderedWhenItWasPublished(t *testing.T) {\n96\t\tvar golden map[string]string\n97\t\traw, err := os.ReadFile(reviewBriefGoldenPath)\n98\t\tif os.Getenv(\"UPDATE_BRIEF_GOLDEN\") != \"\" {\n99\t\t\tgolden = map[string]string{}\n100\t\t\tif err == nil {\n101\t\t\t\tif jerr := json.Unmarshal(raw, &golden); jerr != nil {\n102\t\t\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"the recorded digests cannot be read, and would be replaced by today's: %v\", jerr)\n103\t\t\t\t}\n104\t\t\t} else if !os.IsNotExist(err) {\n105\t\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"the recorded digests cannot be read: %v\", err)\n106\t\t\t}\n107\t\t\tfor _, version := range briefTemplatesInUse() {\n108\t\t\t\tif _, kept := golden[version]; !kept { // a published version is never rewritten\n109\t\t\t\t\tgolden[version] = briefTemplateDigest(version)\n110\t\t\t\t}\n111\t\t\t}\n112\t\t\tout, _ := json.MarshalIndent(golden, \"\", \"  \")\n113\t\t\tif err := os.WriteFile(reviewBriefGoldenPath, append(out, '\\n'), 0o644); err != nil {\n114\t\t\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n115\t\t\t}\n116\t\t\treturn\n117\t\t}\n118\t\tif err != nil {\n119\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"no golden digests of the review brief templates: %v\", err)\n120\t\t}\n121\t\tif err := json.Unmarshal(raw, &golden); err != nil {\n122\t\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n123\t\t}\n124\t\tinUse := map[string]bool{}\n125\t\tfor _, version := range briefTemplatesInUse() {\n126\t\t\tinUse[version] = true\n127\t\t}\n128\t\tfor version := range golden {\n129\t\t\tif !inUse[version] {\n130\t\t\t\tt.Errorf(\"%s has a recorded digest but is no longer a template a run may have been briefed with: runs briefed with it could not be verified or resumed; keep it in reviewBriefEarlierTemplates\", version)\n131\t\t\t}\n132\t\t}\n133\t\tfor _, version := range briefTemplatesInUse() {\n134\t\t\twant, ok := golden[version]\n135\t\t\tif !ok {\n136\t\t\t\tt.Errorf(\"%s has no golden digest: record it with UPDATE_BRIEF_GOLDEN=1 when the version is published, and never rewrite one\", version)\n137\t\t\t\tcontinue\n138\t\t\t}\n139\t\t\tif got := briefTemplateDigest(version); got != want {\n140\t\t\t\tt.Errorf(\"%s renders different text than when it was published (%s, was %s): runs briefed with it can no longer be re-rendered; a change to the text takes a new template version, and the old one keeps rendering\", version, got, want)\n141\t\t\t}\n142\t\t}\n143\t}\n144\t\n145\t// The guard itself: every section of every variant is under the digest, two renderings agree\n146\t// (also across a rebuilt bundle), and two versions never render the same text.\n147\tfunc TestTheDigestSeesEverySectionOfEveryVariant(t *testing.T) {\n148\t\ttext := renderFixedBriefs(reviewBriefTemplateConclusions)\n149\t\tfor _, section := range []string{\"## Structural facts to answer for\", \"SD-bbbb2222\", \"also changed by other-spec\", \"Implementer note.\", \"[core]\", \"round 2\", \"B1\", \"The previous round is run rrn-prior0000000001\", \"draft of round 1 could not be read\", \"none recorded\", \"old.go\", \"(recommended\", \"fence in the notes\"} {\n150\t\t\tif !strings.Contains(strings.ToLower(text), strings.ToLower(section)) {\n151\t\t\t\tt.Errorf(\"the fixed renderings carry no %q: a sentence of that section could change without the digest moving\", section)\n152\t\t\t}\n153\t\t}\n154\t\tif renderFixedBriefs(reviewBriefTemplateConclusions) != text || briefTemplateDigest(reviewBriefTemplateConclusions) != briefTemplateDigest(reviewBriefTemplateConclusions) {\n155\t\t\tt.Fatal(\"the rendering of a version is not deterministic\")\n156\t\t}\n157\t\tif briefTemplateDigest(reviewBriefTemplateConclusions) == briefTemplateDigest(reviewBriefTemplateTypedConclusion) {\n158\t\t\tt.Fatal(\"two versions render the same text: a new version must differ from the one before it\")\n159\t\t}\n160\t\tsum := sha256.Sum256([]byte(strings.Replace(text, \"Map each fact\", \"Map every fact\", 1)))\n161\t\tif \"sha256:\"+hex.EncodeToString(sum[:]) == briefTemplateDigest(reviewBriefTemplateConclusions) {\n162\t\t\tt.Fatal(\"an edited sentence of the structural section did not change the digest\")\n163\t\t}\n164\t}\n165\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"[private-session]","uuid":"2e157bb6-4707-426e-9bbe-d977dfdec9b1","timestamp":"2026-11-09T12:08:25.934Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-4103419841/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_brief_versions_test.go","content":"package pose\n\nimport (\n\t\"crypto/sha256\"\n\t\"encoding/hex\"\n\t\"encoding/json\"\n\t\"os\"\n\t\"sort\"\n\t\"strings\"\n\t\"testing\"\n)\n\n// Spec pose-review-brief-templates-are-immutable.\n//\n// A run records the digest of the brief it was sent, and its proof signs it. The text a\n// template version renders is therefore part of what that version means: change the text\n// and every run briefed with the version can no longer be re-rendered. The text of\n// review-brief/4 changed three times under one version in this repository, before this\n// guard. A golden digest of what each version renders, from a fixed bundle, makes a text\n// change fail the build until it takes a new version.\n\nconst reviewBriefGoldenPath = \"testdata/review_brief_template_digests.json\"\n\n// fixedBriefBundle is a bundle with every kind of content a review brief renders, and\n// nothing that varies between runs.\nfunc fixedBriefBundle() ReviewBundle {\n\tvar bundle ReviewBundle\n\tbundle.BundleID = \"rvb-0000000000000001\"\n\tbundle.BundleDigest = \"sha256:\" + strings.Repeat(\"a\", 64)\n\tbundle.Payload.Scope = ReviewBundleScope{Ref: \"spec:fixed\", Kind: \"spec\", Slug: \"fixed\", Components: []string{\"core\"}, Deliveries: []string{\"capability:fixed\"}}\n\tbundle.Payload.Subject.Entries = []ReviewBundleSubjectEntry{{Action: \"modified\", Path: \"core/a.go\", Class: \"source\", Digest: \"sha256:\" + strings.Repeat(\"b\", 64), Reason: \"changed\"}}\n\tbundle.Payload.Plan.Independence = \"different-actor\"\n\tbundle.Payload.Plan.Criteria = []ReviewPlanCriterion{\n\t\t{ID: \"correctness\", Description: \"The behavior is correct.\", Required: true, Kind: ReviewCriterionKindMechanical, EvidenceClasses: []string{\"unit\"}},\n\t\t{ID: \"design-causality\", Description: \"The design is explained.\", Required: true, Kind: ReviewCriterionKindJudgment},\n\t}\n\tbundle.Payload.Plan.Tools = []ReviewPlanTool{\n\t\t{ID: \"artifact-check\", Requiredness: \"required\", Args: []string{\"pose\", \"artifact-check\", \"--spec\", \"fixed\"}},\n\t\t{ID: \"surface-check\", Requiredness: \"required\", Args: []string{\"pose\", \"surface-check\"}, EvidenceClasses: []string{\"integration\", \"reachability\"}},\n\t\t{ID: \"assess-design\", Requiredness: \"recommended\", Args: []string{\"pose\", \"assess\", \"design\"}},\n\t}\n\tbundle.Payload.Evidence = []ReviewBundleEvidence{{ID: \"core/go/test\", Module: \"core\", Check: \"test\", EvidenceClass: \"unit\", Outcome: \"pass\"}}\n\treturn bundle\n}\n\n// richBriefBundle adds what only some briefs carry: structural facts (one shared with another\n// spec) and a tool scoped to a component.\nfunc richBriefBundle() ReviewBundle {\n\tbundle := fixedBriefBundle()\n\tbundle.Payload.Plan.Structure = &ReviewPlanStructure{Material: []ReviewStructuralFact{\n\t\t{ID: \"SD-aaaa1111\", Kind: \"governance-contract\", Action: \"changed\", Subject: \"an ADR\"},\n\t\t{ID: \"SD-bbbb2222\", Kind: \"api-contract\", Action: \"added\", Subject: \"an endpoint\", SharedWith: []string{\"other-spec\"}},\n\t}}\n\tbundle.Payload.Plan.Tools = append(bundle.Payload.Plan.Tools, ReviewPlanTool{ID: \"assess-discover\", Component: \"core\", Requiredness: \"recommended\", Args: []string{\"pose\", \"assess\", \"discover\"}})\n\tbundle.Payload.Subject.Entries = append(bundle.Payload.Subject.Entries, ReviewBundleSubjectEntry{Action: \"renamed\", OldPath: \"core/old.go\", NewPath: \"core/new.go\", Class: \"source\", Reason: \"moved\"})\n\tbundle.Payload.Plan.Criteria = append(bundle.Payload.Plan.Criteria, ReviewPlanCriterion{ID: \"documentation\", Description: \"The docs say it.\", Required: false, Kind: ReviewCriterionKindMechanical})\n\treturn bundle\n}\n\n// renderFixedBriefs renders a template every way a brief can differ: bare, with implementer\n// notes and structural facts, and as the second round with an open finding of the first. A\n// sentence of any section, in any of them, changes the digest.\nfunc renderFixedBriefs(template string) string {\n\tconclusion := reviewBriefAsksConclusion(template)\n\tvar out []string\n\trounds := []*ReviewRound{nil}\n\tif template != reviewBriefTemplateFirst {\n\t\tprior := &ReviewRun{RunID: \"rrn-prior0000000001\", BundleID: \"rvb-prior0000000001\", Output: \"decision: changes-requested\"}\n\t\tpriorBundle := fixedBriefBundle()\n\t\tpriorBundle.Payload.Subject.Head = \"0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef01234567\"\n\t\trounds = []*ReviewRound{\n\t\t\t{Number: 1},\n\t\t\t{Number: 2, Prior: prior, PriorBundle: &priorBundle, Broken: \"a draft of round 1 could not be read\", Open: []ReviewOpenFinding{{ID: \"B1\", Round: 1, Severity: \"medium\", Disposition: \"blocker\", File: \"core/a.go\", Line: 3, Summary: \"a defect\", Carried: \"F1\"}}},\n\t\t\t{Number: 3},\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\tfor _, round := range rounds {\n\t\tout = append(out, renderReviewBriefBody(fixedBriefBundle(), ReviewBriefKindReview, template, \"\", nil, round, conclusion, nil))\n\t\tout = append(out, renderReviewBriefBody(richBriefBundle(), ReviewBriefKindReview, template, \"Implementer note.\\n```\\na fence in the notes\\n```\\nSecond line.\", nil, round, conclusion, nil))\n\t}\n\treturn strings.Join(out, \"\\n=====\\n\")\n}\n\nfunc briefTemplateDigest(template string) string {\n\tsum := sha256.Sum256([]byte(renderFixedBriefs(template)))\n\treturn \"sha256:\" + hex.EncodeToString(sum[:])\n}\n\nfunc briefTemplatesInUse() []string {\n\tversions := append([]string{reviewBriefTemplateConclusions}, reviewBriefEarlierTemplates...)\n\tsort.Strings(versions)\n\treturn versions\n}\n\nfunc TestEveryReviewBriefTemplateVersionRendersWhatItRenderedWhenItWasPublished(t *testing.T) {\n\tvar golden map[string]string\n\traw, err := os.ReadFile(reviewBriefGoldenPath)\n\tif os.Getenv(\"UPDATE_BRIEF_GOLDEN\") != \"\" {\n\t\tgolden = map[string]string{}\n\t\tif err == nil {\n\t\t\tif jerr := json.Unmarshal(raw, &golden); jerr != nil {\n\t\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"the recorded digests cannot be read, and would be replaced by today's: %v\", jerr)\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t} else if !os.IsNotExist(err) {\n\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"the recorded digests cannot be read: %v\", err)\n\t\t}\n\t\tfor _, version := range briefTemplatesInUse() {\n\t\t\tif _, kept := golden[version]; !kept { // a published version is never rewritten\n\t\t\t\tgolden[version] = briefTemplateDigest(version)\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t}\n\t\tout, _ := json.MarshalIndent(golden, \"\", \"  \")\n\t\tif err := os.WriteFile(reviewBriefGoldenPath, append(out, '\\n'), 0o644); err != nil {\n\t\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n\t\t}\n\t\treturn\n\t}\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\tt.Fatalf(\"no golden digests of the review brief templates: %v\", err)\n\t}\n\tif err := json.Unmarshal(raw, &golden); err != nil {\n\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n\t}\n\tinUse := map[string]bool{}\n\tfor _, version := range briefTemplatesInUse() {\n\t\tinUse[version] = true\n\t}\n\tfor version := range golden {\n\t\tif !inUse[version] {\n\t\t\tt.Errorf(\"%s has a recorded digest but is no longer a template a run may have been briefed with: runs briefed with it could not be verified or resumed; keep it in reviewBriefEarlierTemplates\", version)\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\tfor _, version := range briefTemplatesInUse() {\n\t\twant, ok := golden[version]\n\t\tif !ok {\n\t\t\tt.Errorf(\"%s has no golden digest: record it with UPDATE_BRIEF_GOLDEN=1 when the version is published, and never rewrite one\", version)\n\t\t\tcontinue\n\t\t}\n\t\tif got := briefTemplateDigest(version); got != want {\n\t\t\tt.Errorf(\"%s renders different text than when it was published (%s, was %s): runs briefed with it can no longer be re-rendered; a change to the text takes a new template version, and the old one keeps rendering\", version, got, want)\n\t\t}\n\t}\n}\n\n// The guard itself: every section of every variant is under the digest, two renderings agree\n// (also across a rebuilt bundle), and two versions never render the same text.\nfunc TestTheDigestSeesEverySectionOfEveryVariant(t *testing.T) {\n\ttext := renderFixedBriefs(reviewBriefTemplateConclusions)\n\tfor _, section := range []string{\"## Structural facts to answer for\", \"SD-bbbb2222\", \"also changed by other-spec\", \"Implementer note.\", \"[core]\", \"round 2\", \"B1\", \"The previous round is run rrn-prior0000000001\", \"draft of round 1 could not be read\", \"none recorded\", \"old.go\", \"(recommended\", \"fence in the notes\"} {\n\t\tif !strings.Contains(strings.ToLower(text), strings.ToLower(section)) {\n\t\t\tt.Errorf(\"the fixed renderings carry no %q: a sentence of that section could change without the digest moving\", section)\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\tif renderFixedBriefs(reviewBriefTemplateConclusions) != text || briefTemplateDigest(reviewBriefTemplateConclusions) != briefTemplateDigest(reviewBriefTemplateConclusions) {\n\t\tt.Fatal(\"the rendering of a version is not deterministic\")\n\t}\n\tif briefTemplateDigest(reviewBriefTemplateConclusions) == briefTemplateDigest(reviewBriefTemplateTypedConclusion) {\n\t\tt.Fatal(\"two versions render the same text: a new version must differ from the one before it\")\n\t}\n\tsum := sha256.Sum256([]byte(strings.Replace(text, \"Map each fact\", \"Map every fact\", 1)))\n\tif \"sha256:\"+hex.EncodeToString(sum[:]) == briefTemplateDigest(reviewBriefTemplateConclusions) {\n\t\tt.Fatal(\"an edited sentence of the structural section did not change the digest\")\n\t}\n}\n","numLines":165,"startLine":1,"totalLines":165}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01L5FVXPX5uMB5UP52vgiWiF","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
