gram\": \"go\",\n+          \"args\": [\n+            \"test\",\n+            \"-race\",\n+            \"./internal/cli\",\n+            \"-run\",\n+            \"TestThePickerPreview|TestTheStateGlyph|TestDelegateWatchPicksARun\",\n+            \"-count=1\"\n+          ],\n+          \"severity\": \"required\",\n+          \"evidenceClass\": \"integration\"\n+        },\n+        {\n...\n</persisted-output>","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"[private-session]","uuid":"40c2a1fd-daec-43fc-bf43-b6fff82e3db0","timestamp":"2026-11-09T12:08:27.636Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"{\n  \"review-brief/1\": \"sha256:044c5e094cc0bc9f91268e64c8aa7af3c9e4a941b4d6516c7b2ed2e1b3a4de24\",\n  \"review-brief/2\": \"sha256:de1a8d85203b31bbda2fe4441348abfde0c2bb6b466febdb1a88731c9dfc4d1f\",\n  \"review-brief/3\": \"sha256:36231de8df017908ea02753d257660316d8ffb57f02a4b9e217ec87e4f9fbbfd\",\n  \"review-brief/4\": \"sha256:f6f98745b15e24041ef42b55bf19e4850b72610223b7c7662356a6c4383ab4e9\"\n}\ndiff --git a/.pose/changelogs/unreleased/pose-review-brief-templates-are-immutable.md b/.pose/changelogs/unreleased/pose-review-brief-templates-are-immutable.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 00000000..967a214a\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/.pose/changelogs/unreleased/pose-review-brief-templates-are-immutable.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,6 @@\n+---\n+spec: pose-review-brief-templates-are-immutable\n+category: fixed\n+breaking: false\n+---\n+The text a review brief template version renders is now frozen by a golden digest per version: changing a sentence of a published version fails the build with a message saying that a change takes a new version, and a new version cannot be published without its digest. A run records and signs the brief it was sent, so a text that changed under one version name left its runs impossible to re-render.\ndiff --git a/.pose/indexes/validation-matrix.json b/.pose/indexes/validation-matrix.json\nindex c0710cbc..b79550b0 100644\n--- a/.pose/indexes/validation-matrix.json\n+++ b/.pose/indexes/validation-matrix.json\n@@ -2596,6 +2596,34 @@\n           \"severity\": \"required\",\n           \"evidenceClass\": \"integration\"\n         },\n+        {\n+          \"name\": \"delegate-picker-integration\",\n+          \"program\": \"go\",\n+          \"args\": [\n+            \"test\",\n+            \"-race\",\n+            \"./internal/cli\",\n+            \"-run\",\n+            \"TestThePickerPreview|TestTheStateGlyph|TestDelegateWatchPicksARun\",\n+            \"-count=1\"\n+          ],\n+          \"severity\": \"required\",\n+          \"evidenceClass\": \"integration\"\n+        },\n+        {\n+          \"name\": \"review-brief-templates-are-immutable-integration\",\n+          \"program\": \"go\",\n+          \"args\": [\n+            \"test\",\n+            \"-race\",\n+            \"./internal/pose\",\n+            \"-run\",\n+            \"TestEveryReviewBriefTemplateVersion|TestTheDigestSeesEverySectionOfEveryVariant\",\n+            \"-count=1\"\n+          ],\n+          \"severity\": \"required\",\n+          \"evidenceClass\": \"integration\"\n+        },\n         {\n           \"name\": \"delegated-approval-survives-routine-drift-integration\",\n           \"program\": \"go\",\ndiff --git a/.pose/starts/pose-review-brief-templates-are-immutable.json b/.pose/starts/pose-review-brief-templates-are-immutable.json\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 00000000..485cc311\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/.pose/starts/pose-review-brief-templates-are-immutable.json\n@@ -0,0 +1,65 @@\n+{\n+  \"schema_version\": 1,\n+  \"spec\": \"pose-review-brief-templates-are-immutable\",\n+  \"plan_digest\": \"03339ca50502c234eed0c5990ec38bfb734ada8900794a330901a16f7c0ec375\",\n+  \"revision\": \"cd4baef9c017f113141d26c17f1ca30bda0a69fd\",\n+  \"spec_digest_before\": \"e99d8785cc4c14cd6ea030690035519ca129fc96b3dc12ff6f21f8db0be880e6\",\n+  \"spec_digest_after\": \"3a8c94bf030f8b7e12de8b8f619aa631f0cdd590cd6f207b251adb86d51bab35\",\n+  \"baseline\": {\n+    \"schema_version\": 1,\n+    \"namespace\": \"spec:pose-review-brief-templates-are-immutable\",\n+    \"nodes\": [\n+      {\n+        \"id\": \"R1\",\n+        \"kind\": \"requirement\",\n+        \"namespace\": \"spec:pose-review-brief-templates-are-immutable\",\n+        \"hash\": \"f2db02282564\",\n+        \"state\": \"active\"\n+      },\n+      {\n+        \"id\": \"R2\",\n+        \"kind\": \"requirement\",\n+        \"namespace\": \"spec:pose-review-brief-templates-are-immutable\",\n+        \"hash\": \"4bdc327e6108\",\n+        \"state\": \"active\"\n+      },\n+      {\n+        \"id\": \"R3\",\n+        \"kind\": \"requirement\",\n+        \"namespace\": \"spec:pose-review-brief-templates-are-immutable\",\n+        \"hash\": \"957c1733309e\",\n+        \"state\": \"active\"\n+      },\n+      {\n+        \"id\": \"R4\",\n+        \"kind\": \"requirement\",\n+        \"namespace\": \"spec:pose-review-brief-templates-are-immutable\",\n+        \"hash\": \"af0094ec06a1\",\n+        \"state\": \"active\"\n+      },\n+      {\n+        \"id\": \"R5\",\n+        \"kind\": \"requirement\",\n+        \"namespace\": \"spec:pose-review-brief-templates-are-immutable\",\n+        \"hash\": \"635673f2e3ad\",\n+        \"state\": \"active\"\n+      },\n+      {\n+        \"id\": \"D1\",\n+        \"kind\": \"decision\",\n+        \"namespace\": \"spec:pose-review-brief-templates-are-immutable\",\n+        \"hash\": \"889c952f8a78\",\n+        \"state\": \"active\",\n+        \"relations\": [\n+          \"R1\",\n+          \"R2\",\n+          \"R3\",\n+          \"R4\"\n+        ]\n+      }\n+    ],\n+    \"digest\": \"sha256:4e857b8c652046141e1ee1d8b4c51c1b5185a0f0a74690f91b61f378561c20a2\"\n+  },\n+  \"phase\": \"started\",\n+  \"recorded_at\": \"2026-11-09T10:36:45Z\"\n+}\ndiff --git a/POSE.md b/POSE.md\nindex 12a69511..3e5db9af 100644\n--- a/POSE.md\n+++ b/POSE.md\n@@ -1060,7 +1060,7 @@ Preview `pose review run-sign <run-id> --issuer <name> [--ttl <duration>]`, then\n \n Attach `--run <run-id> --run-proof <proof-id> --sign <issuer>` to a complete `pose review attest` request. The native issuer derives authority principal/execution bindings from the run and signs the exact reference. Criteria, tools, evidence and all ordinary preflight checks still apply. A rejecting or ambiguous draft cannot support an approval; a run-backed attestation cannot predate its completed run or signed proof. Adjudication/smoke run proofs bind their kinds but cannot be used as review attestations. Automatic validation/application of complete typed conclusions belongs to the capability, not to run signing.\n \n-**Conclusions of delegated reviews.** `pose review conclude <run> [--issuer <name>] [--apply] [--json]` records the conclusion of a completed review run: the run's final message carries its typed conclusion in the pose-draft block — `criteria` (`id`, `disposition` passed|finding|not-applicable, `evidence` as `<class>:<ref>`, `rationale`, and `mappings` where the plan asks for structural mappings) and `tools` (`id`, `component`, `disposition`, `evidence`, `rationale`), the brief of template `review-brief/4` asks for them and states the rules the engine checks before it records one (a judgment criterion passed carries a rationale, its evidence is a ref the bundle sealed, a finding criterion names a finding of the draft, structural facts are answered as `mappings`; a draft that breaks one is refused whole) — and the engine signs the run's proof and the attestation with the native issuer, `--issuer` or `conclusions.issuer` in `.pose/policy/delegation.json` (the key stays outside the project), and records it through the same domain writer and preflight as `pose review attest --run --run-proof --sign`. A follow-up finding with `action`, `owner` and `review_by` becomes an accepted risk; any other finding stays open. A rejecting conclusion is recorded too and blocks the scope until the bundle changes. A run that is not a completed review, is superseded, captured no provenance, has an incomplete cleanup or record, carries no valid draft for its round, or whose bundle no longer governs, records no attestation: its conclusion record, in the `review-conclusions` directory of `.pose`, keeps the reasons. A run concludes once: a lock the system releases when the process ends is held from the first read to the last write, concluding it again returns its record, and a reservation an interrupted conclusion left is completed from the attestation it recorded only if that attestation verifies as the run's conclusion, otherwise the run is concluded in its place. Whoever signs it, an attestation of a run briefed with `review-brief/3` or `/4` states that run's conclusion: criteria, tools or findings its draft did not declare are refused. With review policy `delegated_review: true` and `conclusions.issuer` set, `pose delegate review` records the conclusion the moment the run completes; otherwise nothing is automatic. An adjudication or a smoke run concludes the same way, under the same checks, lock and refusals, and never as an approval. The brief of template `adjudication-brief/2` lists the questions the scope's spec records — each decision `D<n>` and requirement `R<n>` — and the pose-draft block answers each in `questions` (`id`, `verdict` holds|does-not-hold|cannot-determine, `evidence`, `rationale`); the verdict is recorded as an adjudication record of the spec in the `adjudications` directory of `.pose`, and `lint-spec` fails, and `close` refuses, on a question the current bundle's adjudication says does not hold and warns on one it cannot determine or on a record that does not verify. The brief of template `smoke-brief/2` asks for `surfaces` (`ref`, `outcome` observed|not-observed|not-reachable, `commands`, `observed`), one per delivery target; the observations are recorded as validation results of evidence class `smoke`, one required check per target that passes when it was observed and is evidence of that target of that spec only, its head, time and provenance taken from the run and the current index, in the `results/smoke` directory of `.pose`, which `surface-check` reads beside the results path, so a delivery profile may demand `smoke`. A verdict that does not answer exactly what its brief asked records nothing; every record is verified on read — its run's proof verifies and it is what the run's draft concludes — and one that does not yields nothing. Runs briefed with `adjudication-brief/1` and `smoke-brief/1` keep verifying with their template.\n+**Conclusions of delegated reviews.** `pose review conclude <run> [--issuer <name>] [--apply] [--json]` records the conclusion of a completed review run: the run's final message carries its typed conclusion in the pose-draft block — `criteria` (`id`, `disposition` passed|finding|not-applicable, `evidence` as `<class>:<ref>`, `rationale`, and `mappings` where the plan asks for structural mappings) and `tools` (`id`, `component`, `disposition`, `evidence`, `rationale`), the brief of template `review-brief/4` (the text a template version renders is frozen by a golden digest, so a change to it takes a new version) asks for them and states the rules the engine checks before it records one (a judgment criterion passed carries a rationale, its evidence is a ref the bundle sealed, a finding criterion names a finding of the draft, structural facts are answered as `mappings`; a draft that breaks one is refused whole) — and the engine signs the run's proof and the attestation with the native issuer, `--issuer` or `conclusions.issuer` in `.pose/policy/delegation.json` (the key stays outside the project), and records it through the same domain writer and preflight as `pose review attest --run --run-proof --sign`. A follow-up finding with `action`, `owner` and `review_by` becomes an accepted risk; any other finding stays open. A rejecting conclusion is recorded too and blocks the scope until the bundle changes. A run that is not a completed review, is superseded, captured no provenance, has an incomplete cleanup or record, carries no valid draft for its round, or whose bundle no longer governs, records no attestation: its conclusion record, in the `review-conclusions` directory of `.pose`, keeps the reasons. A run concludes once: a lock the system releases when the process ends is held from the first read to the last write, concluding it again returns its record, and a reservation an interrupted conclusion left is completed from the attestation it recorded only if that attestation verifies as the run's conclusion, otherwise the run is concluded in its place. Whoever signs it, an attestation of a run briefed with `review-brief/3` or `/4` states that run's conclusion: criteria, tools or findings its draft did not declare are refused. With review policy `delegated_review: true` and `conclusions.issuer` set, `pose delegate review` records the conclusion the moment the run completes; otherwise nothing is automatic. An adjudication or a smoke run concludes the same way, under the same checks, lock and refusals, and never as an approval. The brief of template `adjudication-brief/2` lists the questions the scope's spec records — each decision `D<n>` and requirement `R<n>` — and the pose-draft block answers each in `questions` (`id`, `verdict` holds|does-not-hold|cannot-determine, `evidence`, `rationale`); the verdict is recorded as an adjudication record of the spec in the `adjudications` directory of `.pose`, and `lint-spec` fails, and `close` refuses, on a question the current bundle's adjudication says does not hold and warns on one it cannot determine or on a record that does not verify. The brief of template `smoke-brief/2` asks for `surfaces` (`ref`, `outcome` observed|not-observed|not-reachable, `commands`, `observed`), one per delivery target; the observations are recorded as validation results of evidence class `smoke`, one required check per target that passes when it was observed and is evidence of that target of that spec only, its head, time and provenance taken from the run and the current index, in the `results/smoke` directory of `.pose`, which `surface-check` reads beside the results path, so a delivery profile may demand `smoke`. A verdict that does not answer exactly what its brief asked records nothing; every record is verified on read — its run's proof verifies and it is what the run's draft concludes — and one that does not yields nothing. Runs briefed with `adjudication-brief/1` and `smoke-brief/1` keep verifying with their template.\n \n **Delegated-review requests.** `pose review request <scope|bundle> --kind delegated-review [--purpose review|adjudicate|smoke] [--agents <name,...>] [--note-file <path>] [--apply]` opens an action request of kind `delegated-review` that binds the project, the worktree, the scope, the sealed bundle, the brief, the notes, the policies, the accepted agents and the destination of the conclusion (an attestation, an adjudication record or smoke evidence). No actor answers it: `pose action fulfil <act-id> --run <run-id> --runner agent:<id> --idempotency-key <key> --expected-revision <n> [--channel cli|ci|conductor] [--envelope <file>] [--apply]`, or the MCP tool `pose_action_fulfil`, submits a completed run, and the engine records the fulfilment only when the run is of the request's brief and bundle, of an accepted agent, completed with its containment, its signed proof verifies, its attempt ledger is intact and the engine recorded its conclusion at the request's destination; the fulfilment is verified again on every read. `pose delegate review <scope> --request <act-id>` runs the request's brief locally and submits the run once concluded. A rejecting run fulfils the request without approving anything; a superseded bundle or changed policy invalidates it, even once fulfilled, and it is asked again with `--supersedes <act-id>`, which retires it under the supersession authority rules (`--authority <json>`, `--role <role>`, `--requested-at` from the preview), or, when the plan now reserves the review for a person, makes the person's escalation its successor; a retry with the same key and run is a no-op. A person is asked by exception, as a decision request to the maintainer role: a plan that reserves the review for a person, a spent attempt budget, reviewers in conflict, and a `business_decision` a reviewer raised in its draft. A run's proof verifies in any checkout of the project: the worktree it ran in is recorded, not required of the reader, so a CI job or the Conductor fulfils the request with the same envelope.\n \ndiff --git a/locales/pt-BR/POSE.md b/locales/pt-BR/POSE.md\nindex 64dd9c40..cb4ae3e8 100644\n--- a/locales/pt-BR/POSE.md\n+++ b/locales/pt-BR/POSE.md\n@@ -1057,7 +1057,7 @@ Visualize `pose review run-sign <run-id> --issuer <nome> [--ttl <duração>]` e\n \n Acrescente `--run <run-id> --run-proof <proof-id> --sign <issuer>` a uma solicitação completa de `pose review attest`. O issuer deriva do run os vínculos de principal/execução e assina a referência exata. Critérios, tools, evidências e preflight continuam obrigatórios. Draft negativo ou ambíguo não apoia aprovação; a atestação não pode anteceder o término do run ou sua prova assinada. Provas de adjudication/smoke vinculam seus kinds e não servem como atestações de review. Validar/aplicar automaticamente conclusões completas e tipadas pertence à capability, não à assinatura do run.\n \n-**Conclusões de reviews delegadas.** `pose review conclude <run> [--issuer <nome>] [--apply] [--json]` registra a conclusão de um run de review concluído: a mensagem final do run traz a conclusão tipada no bloco pose-draft — `criteria` (`id`, `disposition` passed|finding|not-applicable, `evidence` como `<classe>:<ref>`, `rationale` e, quando o plano pede mapeamentos estruturais, `mappings`) e `tools` (`id`, `component`, `disposition`, `evidence`, `rationale`), que o brief do template `review-brief/4` pede e para o qual declara as regras que o motor confere antes de registrar (um critério de julgamento aprovado traz uma justificativa, sua evidência é uma ref que o bundle selou, um critério com finding nomeia um finding do draft, fatos estruturais são respondidos como `mappings`; um draft que quebra uma delas é recusado inteiro) — e o motor assina a prova do run e a atestação com o issuer nativo, `--issuer` ou `conclusions.issuer` em `.pose/policy/delegation.json` (a chave fica fora do projeto), e a registra pelo mesmo writer de domínio e preflight de `pose review attest --run --run-proof --sign`. Um finding de follow-up com `action`, `owner` e `review_by` vira um risco aceito; qualquer outro finding fica aberto. Uma conclusão que rejeita também é registrada e bloqueia o escopo até o bundle mudar. Um run que não é uma review concluída, foi substituído, não capturou proveniência, tem limpeza ou registro incompletos, não traz draft válido para sua rodada, ou cujo bundle não governa mais, não registra atestação: seu registro de conclusão, no diretório `review-conclusions` de `.pose`, guarda os motivos. Um run conclui uma vez: um lock que o sistema libera quando o processo termina é mantido da primeira leitura à última escrita, concluí-lo de novo devolve seu registro, e uma reserva deixada por uma conclusão interrompida só é completada pela atestação que ela registrou se essa atestação verificar como a conclusão do run; caso contrário o run é concluído no lugar dela. Quem quer que a assine, uma atestação de um run com brief `review-brief/3` ou `/4` declara a conclusão daquele run: critérios, ferramentas ou findings que o draft não declarou são recusados. Com `delegated_review: true` na policy de review e `conclusions.issuer` definido, `pose delegate review` registra a conclusão no momento em que o run termina; caso contrário nada é automático. Um run de adjudicação ou de smoke conclui do mesmo jeito, sob os mesmos checks, lock e recusas, e nunca como aprovação. O brief do template `adjudication-brief/2` lista as questões que a spec do escopo registra — cada decisão `D<n>` e requisito `R<n>` — e o bloco pose-draft responde cada uma em `questions` (`id`, `verdict` holds|does-not-hold|cannot-determine, `evidence`, `rationale`); o veredito é registrado como registro de adjudicação da spec no diretório `adjudications` de `.pose`, e o `lint-spec` reprova, e o `close` recusa, uma questão que a adjudicação do bundle atual diz não se sustentar e avisa sobre uma que ela não pôde determinar ou sobre um registro que não verifica. O brief do template `smoke-brief/2` pede `surfaces` (`ref`, `outcome` observed|not-observed|not-reachable, `commands`, `observed`), uma por delivery target; as observações são registradas como resultados de validação da classe de evidência `smoke`, um check obrigatório por alvo que passa quando foi observado e é evidência só daquele alvo daquela spec, com head, data e proveniência tirados do run e do índice atual, no diretório `results/smoke` de `.pose`, que o `surface-check` lê ao lado do results path, de modo que um delivery profile pode exigir `smoke`. Um veredito que não responde exatamente o que seu brief pediu não registra nada; todo registro é verificado na leitura — a prova do run verifica e ele é o que o draft do run conclui — e um que não verifica não produz nada. Runs com brief `adjudication-brief/1` e `smoke-brief/1` continuam verificando com o próprio template.\n+**Conclusões de reviews delegadas.** `pose review conclude <run> [--issuer <nome>] [--apply] [--json]` registra a conclusão de um run de review concluído: a mensagem final do run traz a conclusão tipada no bloco pose-draft — `criteria` (`id`, `disposition` passed|finding|not-applicable, `evidence` como `<classe>:<ref>`, `rationale` e, quando o plano pede mapeamentos estruturais, `mappings`) e `tools` (`id`, `component`, `disposition`, `evidence`, `rationale`), que o brief do template `review-brief/4` (o texto que uma versão de template renderiza é congelado por um digest de referência, então mudá-lo exige uma nova versão) pede e para o qual declara as regras que o motor confere antes de registrar (um critério de julgamento aprovado traz uma justificativa, sua evidência é uma ref que o bundle selou, um critério com finding nomeia um finding do draft, fatos estruturais são respondidos como `mappings`; um draft que quebra uma delas é recusado inteiro) — e o motor assina a prova do run e a atestação com o issuer nativo, `--issuer` ou `conclusions.issuer` em `.pose/policy/delegation.json` (a chave fica fora do projeto), e a registra pelo mesmo writer de domínio e preflight de `pose review attest --run --run-proof --sign`. Um finding de follow-up com `action`, `owner` e `review_by` vira um risco aceito; qualquer outro finding fica aberto. Uma conclusão que rejeita também é registrada e bloqueia o escopo até o bundle mudar. Um run que não é uma review concluída, foi substituído, não capturou proveniência, tem limpeza ou registro incompletos, não traz draft válido para sua rodada, ou cujo bundle não governa mais, não registra atestação: seu registro de conclusão, no diretório `review-conclusions` de `.pose`, guarda os motivos. Um run conclui uma vez: um lock que o sistema libera quando o processo termina é mantido da primeira leitura à última escrita, concluí-lo de novo devolve seu registro, e uma reserva deixada por uma conclusão interrompida só é completada pela atestação que ela registrou se essa atestação verificar como a conclusão do run; caso contrário o run é concluído no lugar dela. Quem quer que a assine, uma atestação de um run com brief `review-brief/3` ou `/4` declara a conclusão daquele run: critérios, ferramentas ou findings que o draft não declarou são recusados. Com `delegated_review: true` na policy de review e `conclusions.issuer` definido, `pose delegate review` registra a conclusão no momento em que o run termina; caso contrário nada é automático. Um run de adjudicação ou de smoke conclui do mesmo jeito, sob os mesmos checks, lock e recusas, e nunca como aprovação. O brief do template `adjudication-brief/2` lista as questões que a spec do escopo registra — cada decisão `D<n>` e requisito `R<n>` — e o bloco pose-draft responde cada uma em `questions` (`id`, `verdict` holds|does-not-hold|cannot-determine, `evidence`, `rationale`); o veredito é registrado como registro de adjudicação da spec no diretório `adjudications` de `.pose`, e o `lint-spec` reprova, e o `close` recusa, uma questão que a adjudicação do bundle atual diz não se sustentar e avisa sobre uma que ela não pôde determinar ou sobre um registro que não verifica. O brief do template `smoke-brief/2` pede `surfaces` (`ref`, `outcome` observed|not-observed|not-reachable, `commands`, `observed`), uma por delivery target; as observações são registradas como resultados de validação da classe de evidência `smoke`, um check obrigatório por alvo que passa quando foi observado e é evidência só daquele alvo daquela spec, com head, data e proveniência tirados do run e do índice atual, no diretório `results/smoke` de `.pose`, que o `surface-check` lê ao lado do results path, de modo que um delivery profile pode exigir `smoke`. Um veredito que não responde exatamente o que seu brief pediu não registra nada; todo registro é verificado na leitura — a prova do run verifica e ele é o que o draft do run conclui — e um que não verifica não produz nada. Runs com brief `adjudication-brief/1` e `smoke-brief/1` continuam verificando com o próprio template.\n \n **Requests de review delegada.** `pose review request <escopo|bundle> --kind delegated-review [--purpose review|adjudicate|smoke] [--agents <nome,...>] [--note-file <caminho>] [--apply]` abre uma action request de kind `delegated-review` que vincula o projeto, o worktree, o escopo, o bundle selado, o brief, as notas, as policies, os agentes aceitos e o destino da conclusão (uma atestação, um registro de adjudicação ou evidência de smoke). Nenhum ator a responde: `pose action fulfil <act-id> --run <run-id> --runner agent:<id> --idempotency-key <chave> --expected-revision <n> [--channel cli|ci|conductor] [--envelope <arquivo>] [--apply]`, ou a tool MCP `pose_action_fulfil`, submete um run concluído, e o motor registra o fulfillment só quando o run é do brief e do bundle do request, de um agente aceito, concluído com sua contenção, sua prova assinada verifica, seu ledger de tentativas está íntegro e o motor registrou sua conclusão no destino do request; o fulfillment é verificado de novo a cada leitura. `pose delegate review <escopo> --request <act-id>` roda o brief do request localmente e submete o run depois de concluído. Um run que rejeita cumpre o request sem aprovar nada; um bundle superado ou uma policy alterada o invalida, mesmo já cumprido, e ele é pedido de novo com `--supersedes <act-id>`, que o aposenta sob as regras de autoridade de supersession (`--authority <json>`, `--role <papel>`, `--requested-at` do preview) ou, quando o plano passa a reservar a review a uma pessoa, faz da escalação para a pessoa o seu sucessor; um retry com a mesma chave e o mesmo run não faz nada. Uma pessoa é chamada por exceção, como decision request ao papel maintainer: um plano que reserva a review a uma pessoa, um orçamento de tentativas esgotado, revisores em conflito e uma `business_decision` que um revisor levantou no draft. A prova de um run verifica em qualquer checkout do projeto: o worktree onde rodou fica registrado, não é exigido de quem lê, então um job de CI ou o Conductor cumpre o request com o mesmo envelope.\n \ndiff --git a/pose-mcp/internal/scaffold/dist/POSE.md b/pose-mcp/internal/scaffold/dist/POSE.md\nindex 4382bd4b..065defe6 100644\n--- a/pose-mcp/internal/scaffold/dist/POSE.md\n+++ b/pose-mcp/internal/scaffold/dist/POSE.md\n@@ -1047,7 +1047,7 @@ Preview `pose review run-sign <run-id> --issuer <name> [--ttl <duration>]`, then\n \n Attach `--run <run-id> --run-proof <proof-id> --sign <issuer>` to a complete `pose review attest` request. The native issuer derives authority principal/execution bindings from the run and signs the exact reference. Criteria, tools, evidence and all ordinary preflight checks still apply. A rejecting or ambiguous draft cannot support an approval; a run-backed attestation cannot predate its completed run or signed proof. Adjudication/smoke run proofs bind their kinds but cannot be used as review attestations. Automatic validation/application of complete typed conclusions belongs to the capability, not to run signing.\n \n-**Conclusions of delegated reviews.** `pose review conclude <run> [--issuer <name>] [--apply] [--json]` records the conclusion of a completed review run: the run's final message carries its typed conclusion in the pose-draft block — `criteria` (`id`, `disposition` passed|finding|not-applicable, `evidence` as `<class>:<ref>`, `rationale`, and `mappings` where the plan asks for structural mappings) and `tools` (`id`, `component`, `disposition`, `evidence`, `rationale`), the brief of template `review-brief/4` asks for them and states the rules the engine checks before it records one (a judgment criterion passed carries a rationale, its evidence is a ref the bundle sealed, a finding criterion names a finding of the draft, structural facts are answered as `mappings`; a draft that breaks one is refused whole) — and the engine signs the run's proof and the attestation with the native issuer, `--issuer` or `conclusions.issuer` in `.pose/policy/delegation.json` (the key stays outside the project), and records it through the same domain writer and preflight as `pose review attest --run --run-proof --sign`. A follow-up finding with `action`, `owner` and `review_by` becomes an accepted risk; any other finding stays open. A rejecting conclusion is recorded too and blocks the scope until the bundle changes. A run that is not a completed review, is superseded, captured no provenance, has an incomplete cleanup or record, carries no valid draft for its round, or whose bundle no longer governs, records no attestation: its conclusion record, in the `review-conclusions` directory of `.pose`, keeps the reasons. A run concludes once: a lock the system releases when the process ends is held from the first read to the last write, concluding it again returns its record, and a reservation an interrupted conclusion left is completed from the attestation it recorded only if that attestation verifies as the run's conclusion, otherwise the run is concluded in its place. Whoever signs it, an attestation of a run briefed with `review-brief/3` or `/4` states that run's conclusion: criteria, tools or findings its draft did not declare are refused. With review policy `delegated_review: true` and `conclusions.issuer` set, `pose de","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"persistedOutputPath":"/home/go/.claude/projects/-var-tmp-pose-work-go-pose-review-run-4103419841-worktree/[private-session]/tool-results/b3o5xm1hi.txt","persistedOutputSize":49075},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_014VM4EAfaPKBFmBDRKA7na5","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"subcommandResults"}}]}
